WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:06.875
I was thinking...

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:12.417
You're 17 and you've never had a beer

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:15.667
or any kind of alcohol.
-Of course not.

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:17.500
I'm assuming.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:20.125
But in the tv show...

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:23.250
The beer bottles are filled with water.

00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:29.000
Are your parents proud of you?

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.583
Do they think it's fun?

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.542
I don't like to talk to my parents
about "Skam".

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:39.583
-Why not?
-It's icky.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.042
-It's...
-Why is it icky?

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:50.375
It's uncomfortable that they think
they see what my life is like

00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:52.333
through my character.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.750
How similar is your character to you?

00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:59.833
What a hard question. That's mean.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.208
How similar is the character to you?

00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:08.833
It's very different. I try to use
some of my charm,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.708
some of my coolness.

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:14.500
Other than that it's very different.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:19.625
But the problem
is that they think they see

00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:23.333
exactly what it's like being young.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.333
Not just me, but what
every young person's life is like.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:34.208
"Skam" shows what could happen,
not necessarily what happens.

00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:38.333
Who were you when you were 16?

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.000
What type of person?

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:45.417
I think that's when I discovered music.

00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:49.000
In those days you were in a band.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:55.375
These days you make music
on your computer, but I was in a band.

00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:59.250
We played Kurt Cobain.

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:02.167
It was more punk.

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:07.250
Did you know you wanted to do that
for the rest of your life?

00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:12.917
Yes, but it was too soon to know.

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:17.250
You don't have to know what you want to be
when you're 16.

00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:21.167
There's a lot of pressure
on you these days.

00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:26.833
You have to know
what you want to do with your life

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.625
-and how to provide for yourself,
where to live.

00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:33.375
We didn't think about that.

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:37.667
We were just playing music and having fun.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:41.667
There's a lot more pressure on you.

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:44.625
Just so you know.

00:02:44.792 --> 00:02:48.125
That's not what I meant.

00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:52.750
You have that pressure,
but don't let it get to you.

00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:56.417
That's what I'm trying to say.

00:02:56.583 --> 00:03:02.250
I do think kids of today
are under a lot of pressure.

00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:06.833
They have a lot of performance anxiety
and demands.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.958
But don't worry about that. Just have fun.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.958
Thank you for the question.

00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:22.583
Us parents have also got secrets.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.417
-You didn't see that coming.
-He doesn't find it interesting.

00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:28.458
He doesn't care.

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:33.292
I don't want to hear about it.
It makes me dread growing up.

00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:40.250
Excuse me?

00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:43.458
Being an adult is amazing.

00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:46.750
It gets better.
You get a lot more freedom.

00:03:46.917 --> 00:03:53.500
Yeah, but you guys are winning at life.

00:03:54.625 --> 00:03:57.500
It's not...

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:00.500
Right?

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:04.375
Say that again.

00:04:04.542 --> 00:04:07.667
You are winning at life.

00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:17.500
I don't even know what that meant.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.458
My Norwegian isn't great.

00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:25.542
He says you've done very well.

00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:31.250
You have a job in addition to acting.

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:36.000
-A real job.
-Yes, a real job.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:39.917
I know you love it. What do you do?

00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:44.083
I am a telemarketer. I am.

00:04:45.042 --> 00:04:48.250
I'm selling papers.

00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:52.417
Aksel, have you had a real job?

00:04:55.458 --> 00:04:59.917
-I've been a paperboy.
-There you go.

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:02.042
There's a common theme here.

00:05:02.208 --> 00:05:07.167
-I was a telemarketer.
-You were? Really?

00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:11.667
-Were you any good?
-Yes.

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:16.000
But I told them not to buy.
That made them want it more.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:20.750
"You don't need this."

00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:23.417
It works.

00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:29.375
-Do you want to be an actor?
-Yes.

00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:33.625
What kind of role model is he?

00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:39.000
I told you, he is winning.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:44.875
I also want to be winning.

00:05:45.042 --> 00:05:47.958
But it might not work out.

00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:51.125
Wait a minute.

00:05:51.292 --> 00:05:57.833
You don't need a degree
to become an actor.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:03.417
It's not something he can be.
He is an actor. 100%.

00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:09.375
You're an actor in one of the most
successful Norwegian tv shows ever.

00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:17.250
Thank you very much.

00:06:17.417 --> 00:06:20.583
-You're winning.
-Let's...

00:06:24.042 --> 00:06:30.625
You're the main character in season 3,
which starts in Norway shortly.

00:06:30.792 --> 00:06:34.292
You were the main character in season 2.

00:06:34.458 --> 00:06:39.375
The swedes are getting season one
for Christmas.

00:06:39.542 --> 00:06:43.375
So in a couple of months.

00:06:43.542 --> 00:06:45.792
Thank you so much for coming.

